          "chunk_id": "s03_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c3_parallelism_looks_lot_like_massively",
          "text": "That parallelism looks a lot like the Massively Parallel Computation model, or MPC, the abstraction that theorists use to reason about MapReduce and other distributed systems, where many machines each hold a little data and exchange messages in synchronous rounds.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
