          "text": "Second, the authors introduce a concrete synthetic task, k-hop induction heads, and prove that transformers solve it with logarithmic depth while several competing architectures cannot do so efficiently. They then train real transformers and watch them obey the very same threshold.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
