          "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_trick_captured_lemma_3_2_encode",
          "text": "The trick, captured in Lemma 3.2, is to encode each message redundantly in multiple fixed locations using multiple hashing, and to move information with sparse propagation, which keeps the query, key, and value matrices tall and skinny so the embedding dimension stays small.",
